Enforce PIN access control. Upstream only asks clients to pair: a client can
skip pairing, or call the non-PIN /pair-setup before /pair-verify, and still
SETUP a mirroring session. With PIN mode on, SETUP now requires a connection
that completed PIN pair-setup or pair-verified a registered client key, and the
registration check runs before the pair-verify handshake. Also bounds-checks
the eiv/ekey lengths before copying them.

diff --git a/lib/pairing.c b/lib/pairing.c
index c83200e..0f648fc 100644
--- a/lib/pairing.c
+++ b/lib/pairing.c
@@ -158,6 +158,13 @@ pairing_session_check_handshake_status(pairing_session_t *session)
     }
 }
 
+int
+pairing_session_is_verified(pairing_session_t *session)
+{
+    assert(session);
+    return session->status == STATUS_FINISHED;
+}
+
 int
 pairing_session_handshake(pairing_session_t *session, const unsigned char ecdh_key[X25519_KEY_SIZE],
                           const unsigned char ed_key[ED25519_KEY_SIZE])
